WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.232
Clinical communication changes what happens next. A patient who understands the plan can participate; a receiving clinician who understands a trend can set the right priority.
临床沟通会改变下一步行动。理解计划的患者能够参与；理解趋势的接收医护人员能够设置适当优先顺序。

00:00:11.232 --> 00:00:23.376
Communication can fail even when every individual sentence is true. A report may contain an old blood pressure but omit the newer, lower reading that changes the clinical concern.
即使每句话都真实，沟通仍可能失败。例如报告包含旧血压，却遗漏较新且更低、足以改变临床判断的读数。

00:00:23.376 --> 00:00:36.528
A useful report connects the problem, relevant findings, actions, response and remaining need. Accuracy includes chronology and uncertainty, not just a list of correct facts.
有用的报告把问题、相关结果、行动、反应和剩余需要连接起来。准确性包括时间顺序和不确定性，而不只是事实列表。

00:00:36.528 --> 00:00:47.064
During this lesson, practise speaking aloud. Knowing what each letter means is only the first step; the skill is choosing and delivering the information another person needs.
本课应练习大声表达。知道每个字母代表什么，只是第一步；真正技能是选择并传达对方需要的信息。

00:00:47.064 --> 00:00:58.080
Patient explanations should use familiar words and short, concrete statements. Say what you are doing, why it matters and what the person may feel or need to do.
向患者解释时，应使用熟悉词语和简短具体语句，说明要做什么、为什么重要，以及对方可能有什么感受或需要怎样配合。

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:09.456
A professional report can use precise clinical terms, measured values and times. Replace vague phrases such as vitals okay with the findings that support the assessment.
专业报告可以使用精确临床术语、测量值及时间。不要只说“生命体征可以”，应报告支持判断的具体结果。

00:01:09.456 --> 00:01:22.704
An acronym is useful only if the listener understands it. Expand an unfamiliar abbreviation, especially when handing over medications, an unusual device or an uncertain finding.
缩写只有在听者理解时才有帮助。交接药物、不常见设备或不确定结果时，尤其应解释不熟悉的缩写。

00:01:22.704 --> 00:01:32.184
Match the message to the listener without changing its meaning. Plain language should improve access, not conceal risk or offer false reassurance.
根据听者调整语言，但不能改变含义。通俗表达应改善理解，而不是隐藏风险或制造虚假安心。

00:01:32.184 --> 00:01:44.280
Teach-back asks the patient to explain important information in their own words. It checks your explanation and the plan's usability, rather than testing whether the patient can repeat a sentence.
Teach-back 是请患者用自己的话解释关键信息，检查你的说明和计划是否可理解、可执行，而不是测试患者能否照背一句话。

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:53.352
An example is: I want to make sure I explained this clearly. What will happen next, and what would you tell us if you started to feel worse?
例如：“我想确认自己解释清楚了。接下来会发生什么？如果开始感觉更不舒服，你会怎样告诉我们？”

00:01:53.352 --> 00:02:03.192
If the answer reveals a misunderstanding, explain the missed point differently and ask again. A yes to do you understand gives much less information.
如果回答显示误解，应换种方式解释遗漏点，再次请对方说明。只问“听懂了吗”并得到“懂了”，能提供的信息少得多。

00:02:03.192 --> 00:02:13.200
Use appropriate language, hearing and cognitive support. Teach-back helps assess understanding, but it is not by itself a full capacity assessment.
按需要提供语言、听力或认知支持。Teach-back 有助于了解理解情况，但本身不是完整的决定能力评估。

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:22.896
An open question lets the patient tell you what they think matters. Focused questions then clarify timing, relevant symptoms and immediate risks.
开放问题让患者先表达自己认为重要的事；随后用针对性问题核实时间、相关症状及即时风险。

00:02:22.896 --> 00:02:32.544
If a patient says I blacked out, do not assume a specific event. Ask what they remember, whether someone witnessed it and what the witness observed.
患者说“我眼前一黑”时，不要直接认定是哪一种事件。应询问记得什么、是否有目击者，以及目击者观察到什么。

00:02:32.544 --> 00:02:43.488
Summarize the account and invite correction: the dizziness began while standing, you sat down, and you are unsure whether you lost consciousness. Is that accurate?
概括叙述并邀请纠正：“站立时开始头晕，随后坐下，但不确定是否失去意识。这样理解对吗？”

00:02:43.488 --> 00:02:55.488
Separate the patient's words from your interpretation in both handover and documentation. This preserves uncertainty rather than turning an unclear symptom into an established diagnosis.
交接和记录中，都应把患者原话与自己的解释分开。这样能够保留不确定性，而不是把含糊症状写成确定诊断。

00:02:55.488 --> 00:03:06.792
The AET module teaches radio patches, SBAR and MIST. You need to understand those school competencies and also recognize the current service guidance for their use.
AET 模块教授无线电通报、SBAR 和 MIST。你需要掌握学校这些能力要求，也要了解现行机构指导如何使用相关框架。

00:03:06.792 --> 00:03:19.896
BCEHS A03 recommends ATMIST AMBO for transfer of care in all settings, and SBAR for consultations. It states that using SBAR for other transfers of care is deprecated.
BCEHS A03 建议在各种场景的照护交接中使用 ATMIST AMBO，在临床咨询中使用 SBAR，并指出不再建议把 SBAR 用于其他照护交接。

00:03:19.896 --> 00:03:31.032
MIST remains useful to understand the school's trauma-summary task. In current BCEHS transfer practice, the fuller framework adds identity, time and relevant background.
MIST 仍用于理解学校的创伤概括任务。在现行 BCEHS 照护交接中，更完整框架会加入身份、时间和相关背景。

00:03:31.032 --> 00:03:42.960
Choose by purpose rather than labelling all medical patients SBAR and all trauma patients MIST. A service instruction and an acronym exercise are different contexts.
应按沟通目的选择框架，不能简单把所有内科患者归为 SBAR、所有创伤患者归为 MIST。机构交接要求与缩写练习是不同情境。

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:54.864
A pre-arrival patch gives the receiving team time to prepare. Identify your unit, the intended resource and the estimated arrival, then state the main problem and level of concern.
到达前无线电通报让接收团队有时间准备。先说明车组、目标接收资源及预计到达时间，再说明主要问题和担忧程度。

00:03:54.864 --> 00:04:05.088
Select the findings that explain urgency. Include meaningful trends, relevant treatment and response, not the complete history in the order you obtained it.
选择能说明紧迫性的结果，包括重要趋势、相关治疗及反应，而不是按询问顺序倾倒全部病史。

00:04:05.088 --> 00:04:18.240
State what you need: a receiving clinician, a specific preparation or further clinical consultation through the appropriate route. A long report without a clear request may leave the listener unsure what to do.
明确需要什么：接收医护人员、特定准备，或通过适当渠道进一步临床咨询。冗长报告若没有清楚请求，听者仍可能不知道要做什么。

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:28.584
Use the service's pre-alert criteria and approved format. A radio patch does not replace the bedside transfer report or confirmation that care has been accepted.
使用机构的预警标准及获准格式。无线电通报不能代替床旁交接，也不能代替确认对方已接收照护责任。

00:04:28.584 --> 00:04:37.152
In a consultation, start with the reason for contacting the clinician now. State your role and patient context, then the immediate concern.
临床咨询应先说明为什么现在联系对方。交代自己的角色和患者背景，随后说明眼前担忧。

00:04:37.152 --> 00:04:47.736
Background should be selective. Include information that changes interpretation or the requested decision, rather than reading every item from the patient record.
背景应经过筛选。报告能改变解释或所请求决定的信息，而不是把病历每一项全部念出。

00:04:47.736 --> 00:04:59.256
Assessment includes what you found and how the patient changed, along with actions and response. Label a working impression as an impression, and state what you do not yet know.
评估部分包含发现、变化、行动及反应。初步判断要明确为初步判断，尚不知道的内容也应说清。

00:04:59.256 --> 00:05:09.216
Finish with a specific request. If instructions are given, read back important details and clarify ambiguity before acting within your authorization.
最后提出具体请求。如对方给予指示，应复述重要细节，并在本人权限内实施前澄清歧义。

00:05:09.216 --> 00:05:21.624
This fictional example teaches message structure, not a treatment algorithm. Begin: I am a student with my supervising clinician; I am concerned about deterioration during transport.
这个虚构示例教授消息结构，不是治疗算法。可以这样开始：“我是学生，与督导临床人员在一起；我担心患者在转运中恶化。”

00:05:21.624 --> 00:05:34.056
Add the onset and relevant background, then report the actual observations and times. Saying blood pressure is falling should be supported by the measured trend, not an isolated impression.
补充起病时间及相关背景，再报告实际观察及时间。“血压在下降”应有测量趋势支持，而不只是个人印象。

00:05:34.056 --> 00:05:44.760
Report what the team is already doing and the response. State unresolved information instead of offering a confident diagnosis that the assessment does not support.
报告团队已在做什么，以及患者反应。明确尚未解决的信息，不要给出评估尚不足以支持的确定诊断。

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:56.160
Request the assistance or decision needed. Urgent reassessment and necessary care continue while help is sought; a perfect SBAR must not delay protection of the patient.
提出所需协助或决定。求助时仍应继续紧急再评估和必要照护；不能为了完成完美 SBAR 而延误患者保护。

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:08.520
MIST organizes a concise trauma summary. Describe the mechanism without making it a substitute for examination: a concerning mechanism raises suspicion but does not prove a specific injury.
MIST 用于组织简洁创伤概括。描述受伤机制，但不能让机制代替检查：危险机制增加怀疑，却不能证明某一具体损伤。

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:18.408
Distinguish an observed injury from a suspected one. Report the relevant signs and their direction of change, including mental status and measurements.
区分观察到的损伤与怀疑损伤。报告相关体征及变化方向，包括意识状态和测量值。

00:06:18.408 --> 00:06:29.784
For treatment, pair the intervention with timing and response. Saying oxygen given or bleeding treated leaves out whether the problem improved, persisted or worsened.
治疗部分应把干预与时间及反应配对。只说“给氧了”或“处理出血了”，没有说明问题改善、持续还是恶化。

00:06:29.784 --> 00:06:41.304
In a formal transfer using the current BCEHS framework, add the other ATMIST AMBO elements. The same essential clinical facts should survive a change in the report structure.
按照现行 BCEHS 框架正式交接时，应补充 ATMIST AMBO 的其他要素。报告结构改变，不应让必要临床事实消失。

00:06:41.304 --> 00:06:53.520
ATMIST starts with age and patient identification, then the time of injury or symptom onset. Identify an uncertain onset as uncertain rather than replacing it with the time of the call.
ATMIST 首先交代年龄和患者身份，再说明受伤或症状起始时间。起病不确定时应明确不确定，不能用呼叫时间替代。

00:06:53.520 --> 00:07:01.680
M can describe the mechanism of injury or the medical complaint. This is why the framework is not limited to trauma patients.
M 可以描述受伤机制，也可以描述内科主诉，因此这个框架并非只适用于创伤患者。

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:16.656
I includes injuries and relevant examination findings. S gives the current signs and important changes. Report a measured mental-status assessment accurately; a greeting alone does not establish a full neurological score.
I 包含损伤和相关检查结果；S 包含当前体征及重要变化。意识评估应如实报告，不能只因患者打了招呼，就认定已完成完整神经评分。

00:07:16.656 --> 00:07:25.464
The final T connects treatment to response. A receiving clinician needs to know both what has been tried and whether the patient changed afterwards.
最后一个 T 把治疗与反应连接起来。接收医护人员既要知道尝试了什么，也要知道之后患者怎样变化。

00:07:25.464 --> 00:07:36.696
After the immediate picture, AMBO supplies relevant background. An allergy entry is more useful when it includes the reported reaction, not just a drug name.
交代眼前情况后，AMBO 补充相关背景。过敏信息包含所报告的反应，比只报药名更有用。

00:07:36.696 --> 00:07:48.144
Unknown allergy status is different from no known allergies. Similarly, a medication history that was not obtained should not be presented as a patient taking no medicines.
过敏情况未知，与没有已知过敏不同；尚未取得用药史，也不能报告为患者没有服药。

00:07:48.144 --> 00:07:59.400
Include medical, social or family background when it changes care, safety or interpretation. The complete life history is not required in the initial focused handover.
当医疗、社会或家庭背景会影响照护、安全或判断时，应报告。初次重点交接不需要患者完整人生经历。

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:11.760
Other relevant information can include a communication support need or an unresolved risk. Finish by making it easy for the receiver to ask questions and identify what still needs checking.
其他相关信息可以包括沟通支持需要或未解决风险。最后应让接收者能够提问，并确认还有什么需要核实。

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:24.024
Begin with age, identity and onset: a 62-year-old patient with breathlessness beginning at thirteen twenty. State the main concern without claiming an unconfirmed cause.
从年龄、身份和起病开始：“六十二岁患者，十三点二十分开始呼吸困难。”说明主要担忧，但不把未确认病因说成定论。

00:08:24.024 --> 00:08:36.432
Report the examination and change: respiratory rate rose from twenty-two to thirty, and the patient now speaks in shorter phrases. Add the actual observation times when giving the report.
报告检查及变化：“呼吸频率由每分钟二十二次升至三十次，现在说话句子更短。”正式报告时还应说明实际观察时间。

00:08:36.432 --> 00:08:49.392
Then state the care delivered and its response, followed by relevant allergies, medicines and background. If a medication list or allergy history is unavailable, identify that gap clearly.
随后说明已经提供的照护及反应，再补充相关过敏、药物和背景。如果用药单或过敏史无法获得，应明确说明缺口。

00:08:49.392 --> 00:09:00.888
The receiver should hear a changing clinical picture, not just a string of normal and abnormal numbers. Confirm who has accepted the report and which concerns need immediate attention.
接收者应听到正在变化的临床图景，而不只是一串正常或异常数字。确认谁已接收报告，以及哪些问题需要立即关注。

00:09:00.888 --> 00:09:12.864
Use the full drug name, dose with units, route, time and response. These five facts help the receiving team avoid duplicate dosing and understand what remains untreated.
使用完整药名、带单位的剂量、给药途径、时间及反应。这五项帮助接收团队避免重复给药，并理解哪些问题仍未解决。

00:09:12.864 --> 00:09:23.712
Milligrams and micrograms are not interchangeable. State the unit aloud and keep it attached to the number in the record. Avoid abbreviations that could be misheard.
毫克和微克不能互换。应把单位说出来，并在记录中始终与数值一起填写，避免可能听错的缩写。

00:09:23.712 --> 00:09:37.080
Time is the administration time, not merely when the medication was prepared or the report written. Report repeated doses separately or with an accurate cumulative total and individual times as relevant.
这里的时间是实际给药时间，不只是配药或写报告时间。重复给药应逐次报告，或在适当时准确交代累计量及各次时间。

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:47.040
If a fact is uncertain, say so and verify it. Do not fill in an assumed dose or response because it seems usual for that medicine.
某项信息不确定时，应说明并核实。不能因为某剂量或反应“很常见”，就推测填入。

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:56.136
This supplied fictional record is only for reporting practice. It is not an instruction to administer this medication or a guide to dose selection.
这份虚构给药记录仅用于练习报告，不是给药指令，也不是剂量选择指南。

00:09:56.136 --> 00:10:10.128
A clear report is: ondansetron, four milligrams intravenously, at fourteen oh eight. At fourteen fifteen, the patient reported less nausea; no further vomiting was observed during that interval.
清晰报告可以是：“十四点零八分静脉给予昂丹司琼四毫克。十四点十五分患者表示恶心减轻；该时间段内未再观察到呕吐。”

00:10:10.128 --> 00:10:20.616
Notice that the response is attributed and time-limited. The report does not claim the underlying illness has resolved or that every possible adverse effect was excluded.
注意，反应说明了信息来源和时间范围，没有宣称基础疾病已经解决，也没有声称已排除所有可能不良反应。

00:10:20.616 --> 00:10:32.496
If another dose was mentioned but cannot be confirmed, state that uncertainty and seek the record or administering clinician. Guessing would create a false basis for the next treatment decision.
如果有人提到另一次给药但无法确认，应明确不确定，并核查记录或询问给药人员。猜测会为下一步治疗决定制造错误依据。

00:10:32.496 --> 00:10:44.472
Closed-loop communication checks that a message was received as intended. It is particularly useful for critical details, requests and instructions where a misunderstanding could change care.
闭环沟通核实消息是否按原意被接收。对关键细节、请求和指示尤其有用，因为误解可能改变照护。

00:10:44.472 --> 00:10:54.864
The receiver repeats the important content, and the sender confirms or corrects it. A nod or an indistinct reply may not establish shared understanding.
接收者复述重要内容，发送者确认或纠正。点头或含糊回应未必意味着双方理解一致。

00:10:54.864 --> 00:11:13.296
AET also lists ISBARR: identification, situation, background, assessment, recommendation and read-back. Understand the added identification and confirmation steps without treating this glossary term as a replacement for current service transfer guidance.
AET 还列出 ISBARR：身份、情况、背景、评估、建议和复述。应理解增加的身份确认与闭环步骤，但不能把词汇表中的术语当成现行机构交接指导的替代。

00:11:13.296 --> 00:11:24.648
Questions are a safety step, not evidence that the report failed. If a question exposes missing information, identify whether it can be checked now and who will follow it up.
提问是安全步骤，不代表报告失败。如果问题暴露信息缺失，应确认现在能否核实，以及由谁跟进。

00:11:24.648 --> 00:11:36.576
Before a handover, identify the appropriate receiving person and gain their attention. Reduce interruptions when possible and avoid broadcasting private information to unnecessary listeners.
交接前，确认适当接收者并取得其注意。尽可能减少打断，避免向不需要知情的人公开患者隐私。

00:11:36.576 --> 00:11:47.016
BCEHS guidance describes a brief attention period for critical handovers when the patient's condition allows. It must not interrupt immediately necessary care.
BCEHS 指导描述：患者情况允许时，可为危重交接安排短暂专注时段，但不能中断立即必要的照护。

00:11:47.016 --> 00:11:59.208
Keep the report focused, then allow questions and clarify unresolved risks. Time targets in guidance support communication; they are not a reason to omit a decisive finding.
报告保持重点清楚，随后留出提问机会并澄清未解决风险。指导中的时间目标用于支持沟通，不能成为遗漏决定性结果的理由。

00:11:59.208 --> 00:12:12.192
A bed location or completed radio patch does not by itself prove that responsibility has transferred. Follow the service process to confirm acceptance, document the transfer and preserve continuity.
安排到床位或完成无线电通报，本身并不能证明照护责任已转移。应按机构流程确认接收、记录交接，并保持连续照护。

00:12:12.192 --> 00:12:23.616
Pause and give a report aloud. You have a mechanism and a symptom, but not a confirmed fracture, a complete neurological assessment or the actual observation values.
请暂停并大声报告。你已知受伤机制和症状，但尚无确定骨折诊断、完整神经评估，也没有具体观察数值。

00:12:23.616 --> 00:12:34.272
Do not invent the missing findings. Say what the assessment has established, obtain the latest measurements and distinguish a suspected injury from an observed finding.
不能虚构缺失结果。说明评估已确认什么，取得最新测量，并区分怀疑损伤与观察结果。

00:12:34.272 --> 00:12:48.072
Use the selected framework to order the information. Include the timing, symptom, examination, verified trend, actual care and response, then relevant background and any remaining gap.
按所选框架组织信息，包括时间、症状、检查、已核实趋势、实际照护及反应，再报告相关背景和剩余缺口。

00:12:48.072 --> 00:12:58.776
Ask a partner to tell you the main concern and what happens next. If they cannot, revise the emphasis or request rather than merely speaking faster.
请搭档说出主要担忧和下一步。如果对方无法回答，应调整重点或请求，而不是仅仅加快语速。
